cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "sturm_messageix: a STURM ⇄ MESSAGEix-Austria building-sector soft-linkage"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the accompanying thesis."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hörtenhuber
    given-names: Christian
abstract: >-
  An iterative soft-linkage coupling the STURM building-stock model to
  MESSAGEix-Austria: STURM's final energy converts to useful energy with the
  energy-system model's own conversion coefficients and drives the buildings
  demand, calibration-pinned to Austrian statistics, with prices fed back each
  iteration. Used to study the system-wide effect of building-sector
  digitalization and carbon pricing on Austria's 2040 climate-neutrality
  target. (An earlier per-fuel activity-bounds coupling is retained as an
  archived sensitivity.)
keywords:
  - MESSAGEix
  - STURM
  - buildings
  - energy-system modelling
  - Austria
  - digitalization
license: MIT
notes: >-
  The MIT licence covers the project's own code. The repository bundles third-party
  assets under their own terms (STURM fork: Apache-2.0; MESSAGEix-Austria baseline
  workbook; Macko 2025 dataset) — see LICENSE.
version: 2.0.2
date-released: "2026-09-08"
